  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197200: Bounded multi-connection PostgreSQL pool

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The native pool table may own multiple physical PostgreSQL channels, but guest
Kotoba receives only opaque pool and lease tokens. Host configuration fixes the
maximum pools, physical connections per pool, outstanding leases, acquisition
wait, idle timeout and maximum lifetime. Acquire reuses an idle channel or
grows only to the fixed limit; saturation waits only for the fixed interval and
then denies. No guest-controlled timeout or raw channel is introduced.

Release invalidates the lease before running the compiled Kotoba
`ROLLBACK`/`DISCARD ALL` reset. Reset failure closes and evicts that physical
channel. Acquire/release reap expired idle channels. A replacement connection
performs a new TLS and SCRAM establishment and therefore observes the latest
host credential and trust generations decided by ADR-2607197100.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification opens two simultaneous physical
connections, denies a third acquisition after the bounded wait, rotates lease
tokens, denies close while leased, and confirms reset before reuse. An injected
monotonic test clock independently crosses maximum lifetime while below idle
timeout, then crosses idle timeout while below lifetime; both cases close the
old channel and establish a distinct replacement generation without leaks.

This closes bounded multi-connection sizing/wait and idle/lifetime eviction.
Version/platform compatibility matrices, concurrent waiter fairness and
long-duration soak remain open."}]
